## Why This Is Asked
To probe low-level memory reclamation, cross-VM isolation, and NUMA-aware design under high concurrency.

## Key Concepts
- per-VM quotas
- lock-free data structures and CAS
- host pressure estimation
- NUMA locality and cache coherence
- correctness under rapid churn and bursts

## Code Example
```c
// Minimal balloon path
void balloon_reclaim(vm_t *vm){
  while (deficit(vm) > 0){
    page_t *p = pop_free_vm(vm);
    if (!p) break;
    if (cmpxchg(&p->refcnt, 1, 0))
      reclaim_to_buddy(p);
    dec_deficit(vm);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for fairness across thousands of VMs?
- How would you handle balloon racing with multiple balloon threads?

