## Why This Is Asked
Signals interrupting kernel I/O are a core but subtle area; beginners must reason about races and correctness.

## Key Concepts
- Blocking I/O, signals, race conditions, atomic flags, wakeups
- EINTR semantics and partial reads
- Memory visibility and CAS-based state updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-C implementation sketch for read_with_signal
int read_with_signal(int fd, void *buf, int n, int *interrupted){
  int total = 0;
  while (total < n){
    int got = kernel_read(fd, (char*)buf + total, n - total);
    if (got > 0){ total += got; continue; }
    if (pending_signal(fd_thread_id)){ *interrupted = 1; return -1; }
    // block until wake
  }
  return total;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to handle multiple signals, and nesting of signals?
- How would you test race conditions between signal delivery and I/O completion?

Why This Is Asked
Tests lock-free data structures, cross-core coordination, and end-to-end IO flow. It gauges ability to design scalable, low-latency paths with correct completion routing.

Key Concepts
- Per-device queues and shared completion path
- Lock-free enqueue/dequeue via CAS
- Correct delivery to originating process
- Backpressure, burst handling, and deadlock avoidance

Code Example
```c
// Pseudo-C: per-device ring enqueue
typedef struct req { void* buf; size_t len; int op; } req_t;
typedef struct ring { _Atomic(int) head, tail; req_t* buf[N]; } ring_t;
int enqueue(ring_t* r, req_t* e){
  int t = atomic_load(&r->tail);
  int next = (t + 1) % N;
  if (next == atomic_load(&r->head)) return -1; // full
  r->buf[t] = e;
  atomic_store(&r->tail, next);
  return 0;
}
req_t* dequeue(ring_t* r){
  int h = atomic_load(&r->head);
  int t = atomic_load(&r->tail);
  if (h == t) return NULL; // empty
  req_t* e = r->buf[h];
  atomic_store(&r->head, (h + 1) % N);
  return e;
}
``` 

Follow-up Questions
- How to scale with multiple devices sharing completion rings?
- How to handle out-of-order completions and per-process cancellation?
- What tests validate fairness under mixed device load?

